    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T21:59:16Z",
    "body": "Worker check before code (issue-worker-medium). No claim was made. No branch or code exists. PR #2001 is merged, so the Waterjet pattern is available on `main`.\n\nWhere the wire operations read the wire data now:\n- `crates/app/src/operation/wire_op.rs`: a Wire Contour mounts no library tool.\n- It reads `wire_diameter` and `gap` from one EDM condition of the machine file (`one_condition`, `job_wire`).\n- `job_tool` then builds a stand-in tool from `cond.wire_diameter`.\n- The kerf and the burnout clearance are `wire_diameter * 0.5 + gap` from the same condition.\n- The wire diameter is part of the operation stamp (`wire_op` digest).\n\nResult:\n- A new Wire `ToolKind` that only makes a wire selectable in the library would change nothing for the wire operations. This does not meet \"the wire operations use it\".\n- To meet it, the wire operations must read the wire diameter from the tool. This changes the kerf, the offset and the posted G-code. It also needs a rule for a tool that disagrees with the machine condition (the machine file lists `wire_diameters`).\n- This is under the safety floor of AGENTS.md. It needs a decision, a refusal law and golden outputs.\n\nAction: effort label raised from `effort:medium` to `effort:high`. The issue stays unclaimed.\n\nOpen decision for the `effort:high` worker:\n1. Either the tool is the source of the wire diameter (the condition keeps the gap), and the wire diameter must be one of the machine's `wire_diameters`.\n2. Or the tool kind is an inventory item only, and the condition stays the source. Then the issue \"Done means\" must change.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
